+related:
+  - modules/newsletter
+generated: { by: "human:Urata Daiki", at: 2026-09-29T16:28:17.318Z }
+---
+
+# Newsletter module is kept separate from the application
+
+## Context
+
+The newsletter sign-up feature needs to be self-contained so it can be reused in future products without being entangled with the blog application.
+
+## Decision
+
+The newsletter module lives in `modules/newsletter/` as a self-contained, independently deployable module. Files under `app/` or `routes/` must not import from `modules/newsletter/`. The module exports its public API through `modules/newsletter/index.ts`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The newsletter feature is decoupled from the application core, making it easy to copy into another project. The module boundary is enforced by `bunx guren check --arch`, which will fail if any file under `app/` or `routes/` imports from the newsletter module. This strict boundary ensures the feature remains truly reusable.
